  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing at the Knitting Factory in New York on October 31, 2005 [1]. It is the final night of their Fall 2005 tour, which supported their album Sunset Tree [1]. The lineup included opening acts The Prayers and Tears of Arthur Digby Sellers, who joined the band late in the set, along with a nascent Grizzly Bear as a second opener [1]. The 73-minute set features seventeen songs, including rare tracks like The Hot Garden Stomp and Pet Politics, and concludes with an encore of three songs [1]. The uploader describes the audio quality as rough, noting static and poor sound [1]. One listener called the show amazing, acknowledging the terrible recording but emphasizing the awesome set [2]. Another listener described the recording as perfect beauty and the best ever [3]. A third reviewer appreciated the upload, stating that the static adds charm and that they listen to the recording every year on Halloween [4]. This is the only available recording of this specific date, which is the 91st of 467 archived shows for the band [1][5]. The previous archived performance was at the Bowery Ballroom on October 29, 2005 [5].",
